From: PinePhone firmware
Subject: [PATCH] flex: a column's line no wider than the container

In a flex-direction: column container, a line's cross size was its widest
item's natural width, capped only by the container's own width or
max-width. A container of width: auto (triliumnotes.org's <main>) then had
a line wider than itself whenever one item was, and align-items: stretch
made every item that wide: the page went off the screen to the right.
A single-line container's line takes the container's inner width (CSS
Flexbox 9.4, step 15); capping at it keeps narrower lines as they were.
---
--- a/src/flex_line.cpp
+++ b/src/flex_line.cpp
@@ -434,6 +434,11 @@
 			main_size += item->el->height();
 			cross_size = std::max(cross_size, item->el->width());
 		}
+		// A line is no wider than the container (its stretched items would overflow it)
+		if(cross_size > self_size.render_width)
+		{
+			cross_size = self_size.render_width;
+		}
 		if(!max_cross_size.is_default() && cross_size > max_cross_size)
 		{
 			cross_size = max_cross_size;
